+# @ruvector/core package guidance
+
+Source: `npm/packages/core` in `ruvnet/RuVector`. Maintainer metadata is the
+`author` and issue tracker in `package.json`; do not infer release authority.
+
+Follow the checked-in [shared improvement policy](../../../docs/development/package-improvement-policy.md)
+and repository `CLAUDE.md` / contribution policy. In an npm artifact, consult the
+same policy in the package's source repository at the release commit; the relative
+link above is repository-relative and does not imply that policy is bundled.
+
+## Package contract
+
+- CommonJS entry: `index.js`; declarations: `index.d.ts`; Node requirement:
+  `>=18.0.0` in the inspected manifest.
+- Preserve native loading and the `VectorDB` / `VectorDb` compatibility alias.
+- Platform binaries are optional dependencies. Preserve the exact five declared
+  Linux, macOS and Windows package/version mappings; test each affected target.
+- Consumers pass vectors and search parameters to the native database and receive
+  identifiers / similarity results. Do not replace native tests with mocked passes.
+
+## Validation and rollback
+
+From this package directory, `npm test` runs `node test.js` against a real native
+module. `npm run build:napi` requires the Rust workspace and NAPI build tooling.
+Run applicable native and downstream consumer regressions after code changes.
+`npm pack --ignore-scripts --json` checks guidance inclusion and size only; it does
+not establish that a native binary is installed or that all platforms work.
+
+Record exact source/dependency versions and platform. Persistence changes require
+a separate process-restart consumer test. Keep a baseline and reverse patch or
+revert commit; rollback must preserve stored consumer data. Never run
+`publish:platforms` or `npm publish` without explicit release authority.
